<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Folksinger's Guitar Guide, vol. 2 (Jerry Silverman, duet arrangement and recording)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1964</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gracias a la Vida (Joan Baez, album)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1974</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A chorona (Dulce Pontes)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2006</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Portuguese version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Clear Day (Emilie-Claire Barlow, album)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">French translation with an original verse</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Frida (film, sung by Chavela Vargas)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Coco (Disney-Pixar film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2017</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">&quot;Mr. Ferguson is Ill Today&quot;, Terminator: The Sarah Connor Chronicles (Bear McCreary)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted for the episode</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">La Llorona (film, Jayro Bustamante)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new arrangement with new, political words</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Legend of La Llorona</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the song is derived from it</span></li></ul></section>
